==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|High Speed}}

==Battleground==
*1 [[Gobble]] spawns.
*1 [[Darkmadillo]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 2~3 seconds<sup>60f~90f</sup>.
*1 [[Pterowl Hazuku]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Rain D.]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*6 [[Darkmadillo]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Brollow]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 80~83.33 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,500f</sup>.
*2 [[Gobble]]s spawn after 56.67 seconds<sup>1,700f</sup>, delay 120~126.67 seconds<sup>3,600f~3,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Master A.]] spawns after 73.33 seconds<sup>2,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
If timed right, [[Awakened Bahamut Cat|Awakened Bahamut ]] can solo this whole stage. Simply send him out right after Hazuku attacks to get Bahamut into his blindspot. From there, Bahamut will chain Rain D. and the other peons to death, although you do need to meatshield to protect him. Once Rain D. dies, Bahamut can easily finish off Hazuku with his massive DPS and remove the main threat of the stage. Master A. can be dealt with by disposable attackers like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]].

